# Event log lines are terminated with a single LF by the writer. Never let checkout convert them:
# a CRLF rewrite would change every segment digest and break truncation detection.
*.jsonl -text

# Files the Linux target executes must reach it with LF whatever the editing host does. The
# bootstrap script got there with LF by luck, not by rule, and a CRLF shebang fails as
# `bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M` - a deploy-time failure whose message does not name its
# cause. The worker helper is read by a Python inside the pinned image, which is baked by digest.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf

# vendored 원본은 upstream 의 바이트 그대로여야 한다. 줄끝 변환이 걸리면 세 가지가 동시에
# 깨진다: (1) `git diff vendor/` 가 패치 대장과 일치한다는 확인이 의미를 잃고
# (SEAM_IMPLEMENTATION_MAP §5-5), (2) upstream 과 다시 diff 할 수 없게 되며 (§3.1-1),
# (3) 이미지에 굽는 server_connection.sh 가 CRLF 셰방으로 죽는다. `-text` 는 어느 방향으로도
# 변환하지 않는다 — `text eol=lf` 보다 강한 요구이고, 여기서 필요한 것이 그쪽이다.
# 실측 2026-08-08: 이 규칙 없이 clone 하면 LICENSE 가 1147 -> 1168 바이트가 된다.
vendor/** -text

# Recorded event streams pin the sha256 of this price table with CRLF line endings, the bytes the
# recorded runs read. Check it out with CRLF on every platform so that the checker can verify
# those pins.
config/pricing.openai.yaml text eol=crlf
